  "media": {
    "games": [
      {
        "id": 248,
        "name": "Populous",
        "summary": "Populous is a real-time strategy game where the player takes the role of a deity influencing the development of civilizations. You shape terrain, guide followers, and use natural disasters like floods, volcanoes, and earthquakes to influence or eliminate opposing tribes. The game features an isometric perspective and includes 500 levels (worlds), each with different challenges. Originally developed by Bullfrog and designed by Peter Molyneux, it is considered one of the earliest examples of the god-game genre.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2jjf.jpg",
        "release_date": 613008000,
        "rating": 73.94010846999169,
        "rating_count": 47,
        "genres": "Real Time Strategy (RTS)|Role-playing (RPG)|Simulator|Strategy",
        "platform_ids": "116,149,121,19,29,63,6,86,14,13,16,64",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/populous",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 283,
        "name": "Theme Park",
        "summary": "You have inherited a fortune from an eccentric aunt and her will states the money can be spend building the world largest and most profitable theme park.\n\nCreate a wonderful theme part full of thrilling rides and greasy - but delicious - food and start to make the loads of money. You are a lucky one who can create the best theme park ever made plus make a fortune.\n\nYour park will be compared to 40 rivals all over the world every year. Your goal is to become the best park in all categories.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co9fto.jpg",
        "release_date": 788832000,
        "rating": 68.95389232566134,
        "rating_count": 104,
        "genres": "Real Time Strategy (RTS)|Simulator|Strategy",
        "platform_ids": "114,9,19,29,6,50,14,13,16,62,32,7,38,78,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/theme-park",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 330,
        "name": "SimCity 2000",
        "summary": "It has all the features, flexibility, art, animation, and power you need to create an environment of your dreams. Choose from a selection of bonus cities and scenarios to rule or ruin as you please. Build schools, libraries, hospitals, zoos, prisons, power plants, and much more... Lay down roads, railways, and highways. Explore the underground layer and build subways and utilities without compromising your aesthetics. Customize different buildings or design your own graphics sets from scratch.\n\nThis is the ultimate classic Maxis city-building and management simulation. If this game were any more realistic, it'd be illegal to turn it off!",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co1o4d.jpg",
        "release_date": 757296000,
        "rating": 78.62471912361185,
        "rating_count": 205,
        "genres": "Simulator|Strategy",
        "platform_ids": "19,6,14,13,16,32,7,24,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/simcity-2000",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 387,
        "name": "Final Fantasy II",
        "summary": "The fourth entry in the Final Fantasy series was released as Final Fantasy II in the West, because the second and the third games were not released there at the time. The game is a Japanese-style RPG with top-down world map navigation, automatic leveling up, and random enemy encounters.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2y6s.jpg",
        "release_date": 690854400,
        "rating": 70.16751040651023,
        "rating_count": 91,
        "genres": "Role-playing (RPG)|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "19,5",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/final-fantasy-ii",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 415,
        "name": "Final Fantasy: Mystic Quest",
        "summary": "Focus Tower is the center of the world and balances the forces of the world. However 4 monsters have taken the 4 elemental crystals (Earth, Water, Fire, Wind) for their own use, and also taken the 4 keys that for doors inside of Focus Tower. With the balance disrupted, disasters befall the world. A young boy by the name of Benjamin finds his home village destroyed. Meeting a mysterious old man while trying to escape from earthquakes, he soon learns that he is the prophesized hero and the only one who can save the world. Benjamin must recover the 4 crystals, unlock Focus Tower and defeat the ultimate monster before the 5th crystal, the Crystal of Life is corrupted.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2y0b.jpg",
        "release_date": 718243200,
        "rating": 72.72571927911359,
        "rating_count": 53,
        "genres": "Role-playing (RPG)|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "19,5,41,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/final-fantasy-mystic-quest",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 426,
        "name": "Final Fantasy III",
        "summary": "Final Fantasy III is the sixth main installment in the Final Fantasy series, developed and published by Square. It was the final title in the series to feature two-dimensional graphics, and the first story that did not revolve around crystals.\n\nThe game gives players up to fourteen playable characters, the largest cast in the series, and features the Active Time Battle pseudo-turn based menu command system. A party can consist of up to four characters, though some events require the player to assemble three different parties of up to four and switch between them.\n\nEach character has a unique command ability, such as Terra's Trance, Locke's Steal, Edgar's Tools or Sabin's Blitz, and can also learn Magic spells from earning AP from battles with magicite equipped. Each character's rare Desperation Attack will randomly activate after using the Attack command when at critical health.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/coaq5k.jpg",
        "release_date": 765244800,
        "rating": 89.26498569921357,
        "rating_count": 742,
        "genres": "Role-playing (RPG)|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "19,5,41,137,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/final-fantasy-iii--7",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 452,
        "name": "Blackthorne",
        "summary": "In Blackthorne, players take on the role of Kyle Blackthorne, a lethal commando equipped with brute strength, animal cunning, and a mysterious past that he has just begun to remember. Thrown onto the futuristic planet of Tuul, Blackthorne must contend with a world overrun by mutant monsters and goblin hordes in a valiant attempt to liberate the Androthi people.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co3cuc.jpg",
        "release_date": 780278400,
        "rating": 70.41994808389003,
        "rating_count": 46,
        "genres": "Platform|Puzzle|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "19,30,6,14,13,24,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/blackthorne",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 453,
        "name": "The Death and Return of Superman",
        "summary": "Brace yourself for a hard-hitting fight to the finish that lets you relive the classic DC comic book series! As Superman, fight for your life against mighty Doomsday, the vile distributor of death and destruction! Then, control the destiny of the four Supermen - each claiming to be the one, true Superman! Explode through 10 levels of super-powered battles and fly at furious speeds - until only the real Superman is left standing!",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co25nt.jpg",
        "release_date": 788832000,
        "rating": 59.27159257455927,
        "rating_count": 22,
        "genres": "Hack and slash/Beat 'em up|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "19,29",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/the-death-and-return-of-superman",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 454,
        "name": "The Lost Vikings",
        "summary": "The Lost Vikings is a puzzle-platform video game developed by Silicon & Synapse (now Blizzard Entertainment) and published by Interplay.\n\nThe game features infinite opportunities of retries in case the player loses one of the Vikings.\n\nIn 2015, The Lost Vikings were added as a playable hero in Heroes of the Storm, allowing players to control the three Vikings as individual units, making a unique departure from the typical heroes available.\n\nCharacter abilities:\n\nAll three Vikings (Erik, Baleog and Olaf) have three health points which they can lose by getting hurt by enemies or by falling from great heights, and the ability to carry and use items, mainly keys, bombs, and food (which restore health points). Each of the Vikings has a unique set of abilities:\n\nErik can run faster than the other two, can jump, and can bash through some walls (and enemies) with his helmet.\nBaleog can kill enemies with his sword, or from a distance with his bow (and a \"life-time supply of arrows\"). The bow can also be used to hit switches from a distance.\nOlaf can block enemies and their projectiles with his shield, and use his shield as a hang glider. Olaf's shield can also be used as a stepping stone for Erik to enable him to reach higher ground, which would not be possible without the shield.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co65yo.jpg",
        "release_date": 736041600,
        "rating": 75.99474353612125,
        "rating_count": 89,
        "genres": "Platform|Puzzle|Strategy",
        "platform_ids": "19,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/the-lost-vikings",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 455,
        "name": "Justice League Task Force",
        "summary": "Justice League Task Force is a fighting game produced by Sunsoft and distributed by Acclaim for the Super Nintendo Entertainment System and Genesis in 1995. The Super NES version was co-developed by Blizzard Entertainment and the Genesis version by Condor, Inc. (later known as Blizzard North).\n\nIt involves characters from DC Comics' Justice League, including Superman, Batman, Wonder Woman, Green Arrow, The Flash, and Aquaman.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2wc7.jpg",
        "release_date": 801964800,
        "rating": 44.98569730319048,
        "rating_count": 10,
        "genres": "Fighting",
        "platform_ids": "19,29",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/justice-league-task-force",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 809,
        "name": "NBA Live 96",
        "summary": "As with all games in the NBA Live series you can draft, trade and edit players. Play a full season, exhibition or just the playoffs. 96 includes 29 teams including the expansion Toronto and Vancouver teams.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2do8.jpg",
        "release_date": 812505600,
        "rating": 89.29965189520244,
        "rating_count": 7,
        "genres": "Sport",
        "platform_ids": "19,29,6,13,7,33",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/nba-live-96",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 818,
        "name": "NHL 98",
        "summary": "NHL 98 features much faster and refined gameplay (now using four action keys instead of two, removing the need to double-tap to perform some actions), along other new features such as \"in-the-fly\" tactics developed by Marc Crawford, then manager of the Colorado Avalanche and new commentary lines from Jim Hughson and Darryl Reaugh and a re-worked interface.\nGraphics are improved from the previous version with the players being less angular, and thanks to 3Dfx support, with less pixels showing in the textures. The in-game presentation follows a TV-style script, zooming in players while displaying stats during clock stoppages.\n\nAs far as game modes go, in the year of the first Olympic Tournament with professional players, NHL 98 introduced the first real international competition, with 18 International teams to choose from. Other game modes include Season (option to pick between 25 or 82 games) and Playoff (best of 1, 3, 5 or 7 matches) and a Penalty Shootout mode.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2gux.jpg",
        "release_date": 877564800,
        "rating": 78.7315935702826,
        "rating_count": 23,
        "genres": "Sport|Strategy",
        "platform_ids": "19,29,6,32,7",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/nhl-98",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 924,
        "name": "Wing Commander",
        "summary": "Gameplay consists of completing successive missions and overall cockpit performance affects gameplay: going above and beyond the call of duty results in medals, promotions in rank are awarded at regular intervals, and success or failure on certain critical missions decides the player's plot progress, \"winning\" or \"losing\".",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2khm.jpg",
        "release_date": 631152000,
        "rating": 81.343641458976,
        "rating_count": 40,
        "genres": "Shooter|Simulator",
