      {
        "id": 8775,
        "name": "Micro Machines 2: Turbo Tournament",
        "summary": "Micro Machines 2: Turbo Tournament featured cars that require different handling techniques for each course and also hovercraft and helicopters. There are different playing modes including \"head-to-head\", in which each player earns points by driving a full screen ahead of the opponent. TV presenter Violet Berlin features as a playable driver. The MS-DOS version featured a track editor.\nA selling point for the Sega Genesis/Mega Drive version was the J-Cart, a cartridge including two control ports, thus eliminating the need for a 4-player adaptor. It also included a 'pad-sharing' feature which allowed 2 players to share a single joypad; thus it enabled 8 players to compete simultaneously, on certain tracks.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co4moc.jpg",
        "release_date": 783648000,
        "rating": 84.38726812447841,
        "rating_count": 35,
        "genres": "Racing",
        "platform_ids": "19,29,13",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/micro-machines-2-turbo-tournament",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 8895,
        "name": "Populous II: Trials of the Olympian Gods",
        "summary": "As the offspring of almighty Zeus, you demand a seat among the gods. But before ascending to the top of Mt. Olympus, you must first defeat some of the most powerful deities in the Greek pantheon. Such a task would be impossible for a puny mortal, but you wield the raw power of the universe in your hands, for you are destined to become a god! Learn to shatter the sky with lightning and shower the earth with fire. Summon heroes to aid your people, and plagues to destroy the enemy. Call forth tornadoes, hurricanes, tidal waves, and columns of flame. \n \nThe second installment of Bullfrog's Populous series follows the path set by its predecessor and remains one of the greatest god-games ever created. Populous 2: Trials of the Olympian Gods vastly improves the formula by adding new spells, better quality sound and graphics, and a character development system that allows you to customize your divine powers in any way you want. You really can’t go wrong with a game where you can kill gods, obliterate entire continents, and strike down upon the infidels with great vengeance and furious anger. Just as Peter Molyneux, those things simply never get old.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2by5.jpg",
        "release_date": 694137600,
        "rating": 76.17306987486242,
        "rating_count": 13,
        "genres": "Real Time Strategy (RTS)|Role-playing (RPG)|Simulator|Strategy",
        "platform_ids": "19,29,63,13,16,58",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/populous-ii-trials-of-the-olympian-gods",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 8908,
        "name": "Alien 3",
        "summary": "Alien³ was released after the Alien 3 film. After success on the Super Nintendo and Genesis platforms, the game was built and ported to other systems, including the Commodore 64 and Game Gear. The game is set on the world of the film, Fury 161, but the gameplay has more in common with the film Aliens, throwing wave after wave of enemies at the player.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co47dv.jpg",
