        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 44452,
        "name": "The Irem Skins Game",
        "summary": "A golf game featuring four different game modes. The four game modes are Skins game, Match play, Stroke play, and Tournament.\nThe Skins game has players compete for prize money on each individual hole.\nMatch play involves 2 golfers competing to see who can win the most holes out of 9 or 18 holes.\n\nStroke play counts the total number of strokes over a course of a golf game. The golfer with the least amount of strokes wins.\n\nTournament mode has golfers competing in either one day (18 holes) or two days (36 holes) of golf. Scoring is figured out by how many strokes over or under par a golfer made to finish a hole.\n\nGameplay consists of first choosing a golfer type of either a power hitter, all-around, technician, or magician. Each type has its own proficiencies in the drive, power, accuracy, hook, slice, and back spin categories.\n\nWhen on the golf course the player can choose a club, their stance, direction of where to hit the ball, and the power of the swing. Once that is decided, the swing is determined by a meter which measures the accuracy of the shot and determines whether the ball gets hit straight, hooks, or slices.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co5z1n.jpg",
        "release_date": 720576000,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
