        "id": 134285,
        "name": "Skipp and Friends: Unexpected Journey",
        "summary": "Skipp and Friends: Unexpected Journey is a SNES homebrew (action-puzzle) game that was developed by Mukunda Johnson for the PDRoms Coding Competition (v4.01) in 2009. It came in 1st place out of 8 entries, but the original winning game was not made to work on an actual console. Piko Interactive later reaching out to Mukunda, and he agreed to fix the game and get it to work on the console. It then was released as part of Super 4 in 1 Multicart on December 14th, 2013.\n\nThe objective of this game is to move all three characters to the EXIT in each level. Each character has 2 limited special abilities that you must use to solve a variety of puzzles. The in-game status bar displays the name of each ability and how many times it can be used during that level.",
