        "id": 175959,
        "name": "Yoshi Racing",
        "summary": "Yoshi Racing is a rejected pitch for a 3D game in the Yoshi franchise. The game was revealed in an article by Eurogamer detailing Argonaut Games' involvement in the development of Star Fox where the game was described as a 3D platformer and left unnamed, while a message board post by an Argonaut employee named the game \"Yoshi Racing\" and described it as a character racing game.\n\nFollowing their successful collaboration with Nintendo on Star Fox, British game developer Argonaut Games pitched a 3D game starring Yoshi and made a prototype for it. However, Nintendo did not follow on the offer, with one Argonaut employee speculating this was because the company did not want to let third-parties use its characters. Following this setback, Argonaut decided to retool the prototype as an original IP, Croc: Legend of the Gobbos.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co8jfn.jpg",
        "release_date": null,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Platform|Racing",
        "platform_ids": "19",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/yoshi-racing",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 176042,
        "name": "Kid Kirby",
        "summary": "Briefly revealed in gaming publications, Kid Kirby was a prequel to the Kirby series starring Kirby as a baby. It was developed by DMA Design, who also developed Lemmings and Uniracers.\n\nWhile very few details are known about the gameplay, a former DMA employee revealed official artwork and maps from the game.\n\nThe game was designed to be played with the SNES Mouse, but as sales of the mouse were declining, Nintendo wanted the game to play with a controller instead. The gameplay suffered as a result, and the game was eventually cancelled.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co4au2.jpg",
        "release_date": null,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": null,
        "platform_ids": "19",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/kid-kirby",
        "cached_at": 1772526105
      },
      {
        "id": 176052,
        "name": "Black Out",
        "summary": "Black Out was a cancelled game which would be played using the SNES Mouse. A leaflet about it was included with the Japanese version of Mario Paint.\n\nA prototype (known as Sleep) was found in the Nintendo Gigaleak of 2020. It is a game where you help a sleepwalker traversing obstacles and shooting at projectiles. The game was made to be played using the Super Scope or the SNES Mouse. It has no sound and uses assets similar to those of Super Donkey (another prototype found in the Gigaleak, possibly related to the original Donkey Kong series) and Yoshi's Island.\n\nAs a game under the name of Sleep was never announced nor rumored, even though the game was never shown before and having a different name in the dataleak, Black Out and Sleep they are likely to be the same game given the time frame and the use of the SNES Mouse. Both games are also related to Super Scope 15 (a Super Scope compatible cancelled game) in the dataleak.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co5yux.jpg",
