      {
        "id": 315972,
        "name": "Brave New World 2",
        "summary": "BNW2 contains a total of 100 rooms across 26 exits, with 13 exits for Any% (no secrets/palaces). Most levels are 5-7 rooms in length.\n\nJust like its predecessor, BNW2 is a showcase of glitches that exist within Super Mario World engine.\nSome of these glitches (commonly found in \"Kuso\" hacks) can be extremely precise and require frame-perfect inputs.\nMy intent was to make the execution of glitches as simple as possible while still being challenging and fun.\nThough the custom ASM & graphics prevent BNW2 from being a completely \"vanilla\" hack, the glitch tech involved *is* vanilla and can be reproduced in the base game.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co8s96.jpg",
        "release_date": 1699920000,
